			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Consolidate entry point and improve code quality\n\nThis commit introduces several structural improvements and cleanup changes across the Mountain backend:\n\n### Build Configuration\n- Changed binary entry point from `Source/main.rs` to `Source/Library.rs`, consolidating mobile and desktop builds to use a single entry\n- Added `staticlib` crate-type for Tauri mobile build support\n\n### State Management Renaming\n- Renamed `Extensions` → `ScannedExtensionCollection` for clarity\n- Renamed `PendingUserInterfaceRequests` → `PendingUserInterfaceRequest` (singular) to match actual usage\n- Updated all references throughout ApplicationState, UserInterfaceProvider, ResolveUIRequest, and Shutdown modules\n\n### Thread Safety Improvements\n- **Scheme.rs**: Replaced unsafe static mut with RwLock-based thread-safe implementation for ServiceRegistry, eliminating `#[allow(unsafe_code)]`\n\n### Connection Pool Refactoring\n- Renamed plural to singular for consistency: `ActiveConnections` → `ActiveConnection`, `IdleConnections` → `IdleConnection`, `MaxConnections` → `MaxConnection`\n- Applied across ConnectionPool, Manager, PoolConnection, and TauriIPCServer\n\n### RealTimeUpdate Manager\n- Renamed `RealTimeUpdates` → `RealTimeUpdateManager`\n- Changed field names to PascalCase: `updates` → `Updates`, `subscribers` → `Subscribers`, etc.\n\n### CSP Security Updates (tauri.conf.json)\n- Added `https://*.vscode-cdn.net` to frame-src for VS Code CDN resources\n- Added `'unsafe-inline'` and `'unsafe-eval'` to script-src for extension compatibility\n- Added `chatDebugTokenizer` to trusted-types\n\n### Generated Code\n- Reformatted Vine gRPC protobuf bindings (vine.rs) for consistency",
			"SHA": "134884a4d0a09cc96e90018a177f8be2b6d5131f"
		}
	],
